# Testing Conventions

## Required test categories per PR (Part D)

| If the PR touches… | Add… |
|---|---|
| Domain logic | Unit (D1) |
| DB / Kafka / Redis / Stripe | Integration with Testcontainers (D2) + Stripe sandbox harness (D3) |
| OpenAPI / DTO | Contract test (D4) |
| FSM, pagination, idempotency, money | Property-based with `fast-check` (D5) |
| New route / role / SCA gate / log call | Security tests (D8) |
| Audit, GDPR, retention | Compliance tests (D9) |
| Hot path | k6 scenario (D7), nightly |

## Coverage gates

- Domain services (`cards-svc`, `disputes-svc`, `audit-svc`): **≥ 85% line / 90% branch**.
- `libs/*`: **≥ 90% / 95%**.
- BFFs: **≥ 70% / 75%**.
- Lowering coverage on a touched file fails CI.

## Determinism

- Time: `injectedClock.now()` — never `Date.now()` directly. Advance with `clock.advance(...)`.
- Randomness: inject `Random` — never `Math.random()` directly.
- ULIDs: seeded generator in tests.
- No live network in CI. Stripe sandbox tests are tagged `@stripe-sandbox` and run only nightly.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — flaky, magic numbers, real wall clock
it('expires after 24h', async () => {
  await sleep(86400000);
  expect(await isExpired(key)).toBe(true);
});

// ✅ GOOD — deterministic clock advance
it('expires after 24h', () => {
  clock.advance({ hours: 24 });
  expect(isExpired(key)).toBe(true);
});
```

## File naming

`foo.ts` → `foo.spec.ts` (unit) · `foo.integration.spec.ts` · `foo.property.spec.ts` · `foo.contract.spec.ts`.

## Forbidden

`it.skip` / `xdescribe` / `describe.skip` in committed code · real PII (real emails, real PANs, real phone numbers) — all data is synthetic · `setTimeout` with magic numbers (wait on observable conditions) · snapshot tests that capture raw `correlationId`, ULIDs, or timestamps without redaction.
